-- ls.text --
Usage: rex ls [flags]

List sessions, newest state first. -wide adds start and end times and the resume
id.

Flags:
  -model string   filter by model id
  -short          (deprecated, no effect)
  -show-archived  (deprecated, no effect)
  -socket path    daemon socket path (default $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rex.sock, else
                  ~/.cache/rex/rex.sock)
  -state string   filter by state
  -tool string    filter by tool id
  -wide           add STARTED and ENDED columns

Output:
  -o, --output FORMAT  text, txt, md, json, agent
  --agent              one line per record, no color, no prompts
  --no-color           never emit ANSI color
  -json                legacy JSON shape (prefer -o json)

Example:
  rex ls -state needs_input
