-- new.text --
Usage: rex new [flags] -- <prompt>

Start a session in the daemon and print its short id and slug. Put -- before a
prompt that starts with -.

Flags:
  -cwd string        working directory for the agent (defaults to $PWD)
  -effort string     reasoning effort
  -fleet string      fleet name (optional; groups related sessions)
  -model string      model id within tool (default short)
  -name string       display name (optional; the slug is shown when empty)
  -no-attach         (deprecated, no effect) (default true)
  -skill rex skills  skill from ~/.config/rex/skills to load into this session
                     (repeatable; see rex skills)
  -slug string       session slug (defaults to derived from prompt)
  -socket path       daemon socket path (default $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rex.sock, else
                     ~/.cache/rex/rex.sock)
  -tool string       tool id (default echo)
  -trust             trust the working folder for this session only (answers the
                     agent's trust dialog; nothing is saved, see rex trust to
                     save it)
  -wait duration     how long to wait for the daemon to confirm the spawn
                     (default 5s)

Output:
  -o, --output FORMAT  text, txt, md, json, agent
  --agent              one line per record, no color, no prompts
  --no-color           never emit ANSI color

Example:
  rex new -tool claude -model opus -- fix the failing test
